  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Romans",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 16,
    "summary": "Paul sends greetings to various Saints—He counsels the Saints to avoid those who cause divisions—The Saints should be wise concerning good and innocent concerning evil.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "I commend unto you Phebe our sister, which is a servant of the church which is at Cenchrea:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Romans 16:1",
        "book": "Romans",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "That ye receive her in the Lord, as becometh saints, and that ye assist her in whatsoever business she hath need of you: for she hath been a succourer of many, and of myself also.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Romans 16:2",
        "book": "Romans",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "Greet Priscilla and Aquila my helpers in Christ Jesus:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Romans 16:3",
        "book": "Romans",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Who have for my life laid down their own necks: unto whom not only I give thanks, but also all the churches of the Gentiles.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Romans 16:4",
        "book": "Romans",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "Likewise greet the church that is in their house. Salute my wellbeloved Epænetus, who is the firstfruits of Achaia unto Christ.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 14
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Romans 16:5",
        "book": "Romans",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Greet Mary, who bestowed much labour on us.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Romans 16:6",
        "book": "Romans",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Salute Andronicus and Junia, my kinsmen, and my fellowprisoners, who are of note among the apostles, who also were in Christ before me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Romans 16:7",
        "book": "Romans",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Greet Amplias my beloved in the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Romans 16:8",
        "book": "Romans",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Salute Urbane, our helper in Christ, and Stachys my beloved.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Romans 16:9",
        "book": "Romans",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "Salute Apelles approved in Christ. Salute them which are of Aristobulus’ household.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 73,
            "end": 82,
            "text": "JST Rom. 16:10 … church."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 73,
            "end": 82
          },
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 83
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Romans 16:10",
        "book": "Romans",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Salute Herodion my kinsman. Greet them that be of the household of Narcissus, which are in the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "JST Rom. 16:11 … church …"
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 63
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Romans 16:11",
        "book": "Romans",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Salute Tryphena and Tryphosa, who labour in the Lord. Salute the beloved Persis, which laboured much in the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Romans 16:12",
        "book": "Romans",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "Salute Rufus chosen in the Lord, and his mother and mine.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Romans 16:13",
        "book": "Romans",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "Salute Asyncritus, Phlegon, Hermas, Patrobas, Hermes, and the brethren which are with them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Romans 16:14",
        "book": "Romans",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "Salute Philologus, and Julia, Nereus, and his sister, and Olympas, and all the saints which are with them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Romans 16:15",
        "book": "Romans",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "Salute one another with an holy kiss. The churches of Christ salute you.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "JST Rom. 16:16 … salutation …"
          },
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 50,
            "text": "TG Jesus Christ, Head of the Church."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Jesus Christ, Head of the Church.",
            "prettyString": "TG Jesus Christ, Head of the Church",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Jesus Christ, Head of the Church",
                "entryId": "tg-jesus-christ-head-of-the-church",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Romans 16:16",
        "book": "Romans",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "Now I beseech you, brethren, mark them which cause divisions and offences contrary to the doctrine which ye have learned; and avoid them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 33,
            "text": "GR watch, beware of."
          },
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 60,
            "text": "Acts 20:30 (28–30); 1 Cor. 1:10 (10–13); 2 Thes. 3:6 (2–6); 2 Ne. 26:21 (20–21)."
          },
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 73,
            "text": "GR stumbling blocks, scandals."
          },
          {
            "start": 90,
            "end": 98,
            "text": "3 Ne. 11:40 (31–41)."
          },
          {
            "start": 126,
            "end": 131,
            "text": "1 Cor. 5:11."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "1 Cor. 5:11.",
            "prettyString": "1 Corinthians 5:11",
            "references": [
              {
